The @sine-ai/provider asset contracts are adapted from the structure of
@ai-sdk/provider 4.0.34 VideoModelV4. Asset-specific submission, status,
and polling logic is adapted from ai 7.0.155 video generation APIs.

Retry policy, abort-signal composition, and callback merging are directly
imported from ai/internal through a single integration module. Public
helpers from @ai-sdk/provider-utils 5.0.70 are also used as dependencies.

Modifications include typed asset facades, serializable operation
envelopes, explicit submission idempotency capabilities, remote
cancellation, and URL-preserving results. Asset orchestration remains
part of Sine AI; this is not an upstream generic asset executor.

The reviewed source files and SHA-256 hashes are listed in upstream.json.
See docs/UPSTREAM.md for provenance and upgrade policy. Third-party
dependencies retain their own copyright and license notices.
